#
# Conformance case: foundation/relcomp-under-mediated
# AC: foundation lowering — the OntoUML RelComp discipline, read by ENTITY count.
#
# A concrete relator must mediate at least two distinct ENTITIES. Mediation is carried
# by role properties (logic:mediates names each role); a functional role reaches one
# entity (one end), a non-functional role reaches two or more (two ends). So a relator
# is degenerate iff it reaches fewer than two entities — a single functional role.
#   * ex:Marriage   — a concrete logic:Relator (no logic: subclass) mediating a single
#     FUNCTIONAL role (ex:spouse): one end → logic:RelComp.
#   * ex:Employment — a well-formed concrete logic:Relator mediating TWO DISTINCT roles
#     (ex:employer, ex:employee): two ends → trips nothing (negative control).
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so the schema facts (the
# Relator puns, the logic:mediates edges, and the owl:FunctionalProperty type on
# ex:spouse) are duplicated there in the named world ex:schema; these declarations are
# the program axioms the projections need.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/foundation/relcomp-under-mediated/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix owl:   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

# Schema: an under-mediated relator and a well-formed one (also world facts in input.nq).
ex:Marriage   a logic:Relator ;
    logic:mediates ex:spouse .
ex:spouse a owl:FunctionalProperty .
ex:Employment a logic:Relator ;
    logic:mediates ex:employer, ex:employee .
